# The build context is the workspace, and `target/` is the one directory that would dwarf it.
# Everything excluded here is either rebuilt in the image or has no business in it.
target/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.nx/
**/__pycache__/
*.env
.env

# Not inputs to `cargo build`. The CRM example in particular carries a UI with its own toolchain,
# and none of it reaches the two binaries this image ships. Nothing in `crates/` reaches a `.md`
# with `include_str!`, so dropping the root ones costs no build — only this pattern is not
# recursive, so the crates' own docs stay regardless.
examples/
scenarios/
*.md
